presentations.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_8"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"contents": [{"content": "childhood", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the period of time when a person is a child", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: He felt this bridge reminds him of his childhood.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le10ob09aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about past experiences.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to remind", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to make someone think about something again", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The bridge reminded the man of his own childhood.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le10ob09aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to establish", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to begin or create something that is meant to last for a long time", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: His grandparents worked hard to establish a good life for their family.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le10ob09aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "kid", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a young person; informal word for \"child\"", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: He remembers good times when he was a kid.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le10ob09aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to play a role", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to take or play an active part in something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The boy was told to play a role in where his country is heading.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le10ob09aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to run around", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to run from one place to another playfully with no particular purpose.", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: He use to run around outside a lot as a kid.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le10ob09aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Since When?", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the preposition <span class=\"strong\">for</span> with a period of time, for example: a few days, half an hour, two years.<br>   You use the preposition <span class=\"strong\">since</span> with the time when the action started, for example: <span class=\"italic\">Last year, June 8, I met you.</span> ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "They have worked hard <span class=\"strong\">since</span> then to establish a good life for their family. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "He has read stories about the American Revolution <span class=\"strong\">since</span> I was a kid. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I have read at night <span class=\"strong\">for</span> 6 years.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Used to and Would for Past Habits ", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use used to to express a past action and/or a state.<br>  <span class=\"strong\">Examples:</span> <br> <span class=\"italic\">When I was a child, my father used to take me on walks across this bridge.</span> (action) <br> <span class=\"italic\">We used to live in Cambridge.</span> (state) <br><br>  Notice that in the negative and the question forms you do not use  the <span class=\"italic\">d</span>.<br>  <span class=\"strong\">Examples:</span> <br> <span class=\"italic\">Which park did you use to go? <br> My mother didn't use to read a lot of stories.</span><br> <br>  You cannot use used to with a time reference + a number. <br> <span class=\"strong\">Incorrect:</span>  <br> <span class=\"italic\">I used to spend time with my grandparents in Cambridge for 5 years.</span> <br> <span class=\"strong\">Correct:</span>  <br> <span class=\"italic\">I used to spend time with my grandparents in Cambridge every day.</span> <br><br>  When you express a series of past actions, you start with used to, then continue with would. <br> <span class=\"strong\">Example:</span> <br>  <span class=\"italic\">When I was a child, we used to walk in the park. We would play there, and we would throw one small stone into the river.<span><br><br><span class=\"italic\">Would</span> is not used unless you know that the time frame is in the past, while <span class=\"italic\">used to</span> does not require this.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Used to\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Would\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">My grandfather used to take me on walks across this bridge. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">We would each throw one small stone into the river.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">He has read me stories since I was a kid. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">We would go to the library once a week.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"content": "engenn6le10ob09re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Create a dialogue of 10 lines with your partner about a childhood experience each of you has had with a grandparent or parent.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Talk about the experience in detail. Use the Present Perfect tense.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Talk about what you used to do or any routine you had together.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Practice the dialogue several times aloud with your partner.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I write a dialogue about a childhood experience.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I apply the proper action words about a past experience.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I express past habits or routine.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I practice the dialogue with my partner.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "contents": [{}], "_data": [], "id": 0, "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "title": "", "type": "audio", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"image": "engenn6le10ob09re2img01.jpg", "time": "0", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"image": "engenn6le10ob09re2img01.jpg", "time": "100", "id": 1, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: Oh, this bridge reminds me of my childhood. My grandfather used to take me on walks across this bridge. We would each throw one small stone into the river.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: My father used to take me to the park, but I haven't spent much time with my grandparents. They used to visit Cambridge only on holiday weekends.<br>"}, {"image": "engenn6le10ob09re2img05.jpg", "time": "18500", "id": 2, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: My grandparents were newcomers to the U.S. They came to the U.S. soon after they were married. They have worked hard since then to establish a good life for their family.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: You told me that your grandfather wanted you to learn the history of the country.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: He used to tell me, \u201cIf you know where this country has come from, you can play a strong role in where it's going.\u201d He has read me stories about the American Revolution since I was a kid. We would go to the library once a week, and he would help me pick out a book."}, {"image": "engenn6le10ob09re2img02.jpg", "time": "50000", "id": 3, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: So, you used to read lot in your free time and watch baseball games on TV?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>:  Yeah! And I ran around outside.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Well, I certainly learned a lot about Boston's history from you."}], "audiosrc": "engenn6le10ob09re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn6le10ob09re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "id": 1}], "exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": " I can talk about family life.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about people's past habits.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can discuss experiences I've had or haven't had.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " Have you spent much time with your grandparents?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " Do you remember things they used to tell you?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " What experiences have you had together?", "type": "Free Header Item"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}], "type": "group"}, {"content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "allowed_attempts": 2}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": "Ask your partner:", "type": "free_header_text"}, {"content": "We learn from our elders.", "type": "free_type_text_area"}], "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "id": 0, "img_path": "",